<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Trips</span>
<h1>Hanoi to Ba Vi by Motorbike: Safety Checklist | Hanoi Motorbike Guide</h1>
<p>Long motorbike days do not usually go wrong in one dramatic moment, they go wrong in the accumulation of small unmade checks, a brake that was always a little soft, a route fact that expired last month, a phone that started the day at forty percent. The Ba Vi ride, with its long plain, its climb and its long return, rewards riders who treat safety as a checklist rather than a mood, and this guide is that checklist, written to be run the evening before and again in the morning.</p>
<p>The machine half of the checklist can be run at Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, Hanoi, open daily 09:00 to 21:00, where the desk hands over western-trip bikes daily and answers the safety questions this guide raises. Start at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/">Hanoi motorbike trips</a> hub, read the parent <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/hanoi-to-ba-vi-motorbike-route/">Ba Vi route guide</a>, see the fleet and the terms on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> page, review the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a> for riding and safety, and keep <a href="/renting-a-motorbike-in-vietnam/">renting a motorbike in Vietnam</a> open for the legal layer.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#sec-1">Why A Checklist Beats A Feeling</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-2">The Bike Checks At Handover</a></li>
